<item>
            <title>[MAHOUT-2207] Qumat allowed python versions incompatible with latest cirq requirements</title>
                <link>https://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/MAHOUT-2207</link>
                <project id="12310751" key="MAHOUT">Mahout</project>
                    <description>&lt;p&gt;When running poetry install on the latest qumat, I get the following error:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;blockquote&gt;&lt;p&gt;The current project&apos;s supported Python range (&amp;gt;=3.8,&amp;lt;4.0) is not compatible with some of the required packages Python requirement:&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&#160;&#160;- cirq requires Python &amp;gt;=3.9.0, so it will not be satisfied for Python &amp;gt;=3.8,&amp;lt;3.9.0&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/blockquote&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This is because cirq 1.3.0 requires python &amp;gt;= 3.9.0 and the current poetry.toml specifies python=&quot;^3.8&quot;&lt;/p&gt;</description>
